WEBVTT

00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:16,280
Could you tell me again why a cancer patient should not take glutamine?

00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:20,680
My other doctor wants me to take it for my gut.

00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:31,940
Well this is a kind of a caution for taking advice from too many people sometimes because

00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:39,740
sometimes another doctor is not necessarily trained in taking care of cancer patients.

00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:45,320
So this is why I also ask you, you're free to do whatever you want as far as supplements

00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:49,640
that you feel like you want to take or avoid other doctors and getting their advice by

00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:52,840
all means, go ahead and do all that.

00:00:52,840 --> 00:01:01,880
But I think it's a good idea to run it by me like this person did by asking me this question.

00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:07,080
My other doctor wants me to take glutamine and I think I remember you saying it's not a good idea.

00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:13,080
Well the reason why it's typically not a good idea is because cancer is always trying to find a source of fuel.

00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:18,580
Now the first source of fuel for every cancer is going to be sugar breaks down into glucose.

00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:26,080
Glucose is going to be the main source of fuel because it is always the main source of fuel for all cells.

00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:33,080
Now glutamine is a number secondary source of fuel for all cells on brain cells.

00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:39,580
Glutamine can be primary source of fuel for certain brain cells, especially astrocytes.

00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,580
And your brain can be fueled by cancer.

00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:51,580
So certain brain cancers, especially astrocytoma and another possibility is a glioblastoma

00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:54,480
or can be fueled by glutamine.

00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:58,480
So you have to be careful under glutamine intake.

00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,380
So why would a person take glutamine?

00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:04,780
Why would you be recommended glutamine for the gut?

00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:12,280
Because glutamine can help the help replenish and heal epithelial cells quite quickly

00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:19,580
because it really up regulates the growth of and reproduction of epithelial cells.

00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:26,080
So if you have a cancer, do you want something that's going to fuel growth?

00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,580
Not such a good idea.

00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:33,080
So I wouldn't take glutamine as a supplement to help heal the gut.

00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:35,580
There's a lot of other choices out there.

00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:41,080
So there's a lot of different supplements that you can do to help heal the gut without having to take glutamine.

00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,580
So that's why I wouldn't do it.

00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:46,580
Is that it up regulates growth?

